IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `fa-families`

-- A New Tax System (Family Assistance) Act 1999, ss 6, 21, 22, 58AA, 61B, 85BA, Sch 1 cll 1-3, 7, 25, 25D, 28, 35A, 38L-38N and Sch 2 cll 2, 3, 11, 12 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_a-new-tax-system-family-assistance-act-1999.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

-- Dollar figures: where a case uses a printed Schedule figure ($4,292.40, $737.30, $40,000, $98,988, $500, $80,000) it is the
-- figure AS PRINTED in Compilation No. 124. Schedule 4 indexes each of them, so none is the figure paid in 2030.
-- Scenario facts: Oliver (chloe c064-c066), Ruby and Tahlia (jake k054), Priya and Daniel (daniel d040). The scenarios do not give
-- incomes or hours of care; where a case needs one it is a stated assumption.

§ `Fixtures`

`Oliver, immunised on the schedule` MEANS `Immunisation facts` WITH
    `immunised under a standard or catch up schedule` IS TRUE
    `medical contraindication certified` IS FALSE
    `natural immunity certified` IS FALSE
    `in an approved vaccine study` IS FALSE
    `vaccine temporarily unavailable as s 6(4) requires` IS FALSE
    `vaccinated overseas as s 6(5) requires` IS FALSE
    `the Secretary has determined it` IS FALSE
    `the parent objects to vaccination` IS FALSE

